From: nwrt Xiaomi 14 Pro support <ning@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nas: add Bind Subscription request

Qualcomm dual-SIM modems require each NAS client to select the modem stack it
will control.  The request is part of Qualcomm's public Gobi API description
but is not modelled by libqmi 1.38.  Add the request so the Xiaomi qcom-soc
plugin can bind its NAS client to the subscription selected by the user.

The wire format follows the Gobi API definition: message 0x0045 with mandatory
TLV 0x01 containing a one-byte subscription type (0 primary, 1 secondary,
2 tertiary).

--- a/data/qmi-service-nas.json
+++ b/data/qmi-service-nas.json
@@ -2281,6 +2281,19 @@
                      "format"        : "guint32",
                      "public-format" : "QmiNasNetworkNameSource" } ] },
 
+  // *********************************************************************************
+  {  "name"    : "Bind Subscription",
+     "type"    : "Message",
+     "service" : "NAS",
+     "id"      : "0x0045",
+     "since"   : "1.38",
+     "input"   : [ { "name"   : "Subscription Type",
+                     "id"     : "0x01",
+                     "type"   : "TLV",
+                     "since"  : "1.38",
+                     "format" : "guint8" } ],
+     "output"  : [ { "common-ref" : "Operation Result" } ] },
+
   // *********************************************************************************
   {  "name"    : "Network Time",
      "type"    : "Indication",
